memhouse — tags and their changes
==================================

Generated 2026-10-08 from `git tag` and CHANGELOG.md. 47 tags: 45 releases, plus 2
non-release tags. The 0.17.1 entry comes from the v0.17.1 tag, because that release shipped
on the retired release/0.17 line and is not in main's CHANGELOG. For 0.3.x and 0.4.x, the
CHANGELOG has one grouped section per series, so this file uses each tag's message.
CHANGELOG.md has the full text; from 0.18.10 on, docs/releases/ has one document per
release.


Unreleased — 0.18.10 (PR #16, not yet tagged)
---------------------------------------------
- A scoped share now shares only what its scope filters.
- `--revoke` withdraws the grant before it drops the filters.
- `--only ""` is refused.
- The permissive-server check before a scoped share actually runs.
- An admin password never has to go on the command line. `--admin-password` is
  deprecated, and removed in 0.19.0.
- The admin credential is not saved unless `--keep-admin`.
- Daemons never carry the admin credential.


0.18.x — one layout, team channel
---------------------------------

v0.18.9   2026-09-22
- The Sessions page no longer renders blank on a house with ~900+ sessions.
- An error with no message now says something.

v0.18.8   2026-09-22
- A growing session re-ships only its tail.

v0.18.7   2026-09-19
- `status` and `doctor` say when an update is out.

v0.18.6   2026-09-19
- An upgrade no longer leaves a broken window.
- A converted house is complete when `convert` finishes.
- The dashboard adopts a moved house.
- A machine keeps its host identity across reinstalls.

v0.18.5   2026-09-18
- One release line.
- `memhouse convert`: an operator moves a pre-one-layout house to the one layout.
- A member's env file repairs itself after the move.

v0.18.4   2026-09-17
- `memhouse update` never crosses release lines on its own.
- `install --env` keeps the invite's channel, editors and roots.

v0.18.3   2026-09-17
- Folded subagent turns say which subagent they came from.
- Workflow-run agents ship.
- Bare `memhouse` beside an invite offers to process it.
- A playbook is bound to the instance that installed its plugin.
- The dashboard reads precomputed rollups.
- Every endpoint issues its reads in one round trip.
- `/api/chats` prices the page, not the house.

v0.18.2   2026-09-11
- The shipper spawned by `install --env` holds the rotated password.
- `status` and `doctor` read the shipper log's last pass.

v0.18.1   2026-09-08
- `memhouse instance`: which memhouse this is, on one screen.
- Playbook binding: `plugins install` stamps MEMHOUSE_HOME / MEMHOUSE_BIN into the
  playbook's settings.
- Bare `memhouse` beside an `invite-<name>.env` offers to join.

v0.18.0   2026-09-08   (16 items; main ones)
- One layout: rooms are `mem.<member>_*`, one grant per member.
- One provisioning plan.
- Standalone is a team of one.
- The bookkeeping rooms are `<member>_meta` and `<member>_events`.
- You can choose which sessions ship.
- `memhouse update` follows the channel the install came from.
- `invite` writes MEMHOUSE-INVITATION.md beside the credential.
- Houses from before this layout are refused, loudly.


0.17.x and earlier
------------------

v0.17.1   2026-09-15   (release/0.17 line)
- The dashboard reads precomputed rollups.
- Every endpoint issues its reads in one round trip.
- `/api/chats` prices the page, not the house.
- `install` and `update` create the rollups.

v0.17.0   2026-08-25
- `memhouse share`: partial sharing, by row policy.
- The /mem:* skillset is five skills and one shared reference, down from ten.
- The data model is written once, in reference/HOUSE.md.
- /mem:recall restores a name the canon already carried.
- The CLI no longer advertises a directory as a skill.

v0.16.0   2026-08-24
- An unknown option stops the run instead of being ignored.
- `whoami --admin` says when it fell back.

v0.15.0   2026-08-24
- `memhouse whoami`: which credential is in play, and what it may actually do.
- Capability detection is scope-aware, and shared.
- /mem:admin stops inventing places to keep an admin password.

v0.14.0   2026-08-24
- An unreachable `--url` says so, instead of blaming your privileges.
- `--admin-password` is prompted for when omitted.

v0.13.0   2026-08-23
- New skill: /mem:admin.
- /mem:invite now finishes the handoff.
- `memhouse invite` refuses a house that already holds someone's messages.
- `memhouse relocate` needs GRANT REMOTE ON *.*, and no bootstrap granted it.

v0.12.7   2026-08-20
- A member fully owns their house: GRANT ALL ON <db>.* ... WITH GRANT OPTION.
  The one layout in 0.18 replaced this.

v0.12.6   2026-08-20
- Members can see who else is on the ClickHouse (SHOW USERS).
- The plugin nudges you when the client is behind.

v0.12.5   2026-08-20
- `memhouse update` refreshes the Claude plugin too.

v0.12.4   2026-08-20
- Inserts are gzip-compressed and capped by bytes, so the shipper stops choking slow
  links.

v0.12.3   2026-08-20
- `install` no longer blocks on the first ship; it ships in the background.

v0.12.2   2026-08-20
- The Claude plugin reports the real version.

v0.12.1   2026-08-20
- The skills no longer fall back to a hardcoded `mem` house.

v0.12.0   2026-08-20
- `memhouse relocate --to <url>`: moves a whole house to a new ClickHouse,
  server-to-server, with no re-ingest.

v0.11.3   2026-08-20
- Read a friend's shared memory by naming their house.

v0.11.2   2026-08-20
- /mem:hello leads with a what-is overview.
- The tour separates the three retrieval skills.

v0.11.1   2026-08-20
- Upgrading from 0.9.x needs one manual step: `memhouse migrate`.

v0.11.0   2026-08-20   (the invite plane)
- `memhouse invite <name>`.
- `memhouse install --env <file>`.
- `memhouse passwd`, and self-service password rotation.
- `memhouse invite` uses your own credential when it can.
- /mem:invite and /mem:hello.

v0.10.0   2026-08-20   (17 items; main ones)
- DELETE FROM is gone from the shipper.
- `epoch` joins `origin` in the sorting key, and reads show one parse per session.
- `memhouse migrate`; `memhouse update` names, asks about, or runs pending migrations.
- `memhouse uninstall` asks first.
- `memhouse nightly [--out DIR]`.
- /mem:share and /mem:users.

v0.9.0    2026-08-16
- `--allow-scripts=better-sqlite3` is retired: SQLite now comes from node:sqlite.
- `engines` moves to node >=24.

v0.8.0    2026-08-14
- Provenance is two columns no client can fake: user_id and host.
- Joining any ClickHouse takes two statements.

v0.7.1    2026-08-13
- A single per-user pin, `async_insert = 0 CONST`, replaces the shared settings
  profile; the profile detached members on every provision.
- `install` no longer reports a user it just created as "already exists".

v0.7.0    2026-08-12
- `uninstall` has three tiers: the default, `--credentials`, and `--full-removal`.
- The host identity is a random per-install fingerprint, not a derived id.

v0.6.0    2026-08-12
- Every path that existed only for versions nobody ran is deleted.

v0.5.0    2026-08-12
- `memhouse resume <session-id>` prints the command that reopens a session.
- `memhouse update` restarts daemons and checks the schema.
- Daemons detect their own upgrade and hand over.
- `plugins install claude` acts on every Claude Code config dir on the machine.

v0.4.6    2026-08-11
- Three acceptance rounds against the previous round's fixes.

v0.4.5    2026-08-10
- Twenty-one defects found by an end-to-end acceptance run.

v0.4.4    2026-08-10
- The shipper must not destroy rows it did not write: the `origin` guarantee.

v0.4.3    2026-08-09
- A rendered install prompt, and adapters that degrade one at a time.

v0.4.2    2026-08-09
- The first published release with per-member rooms.

v0.4.1    2026-08-06
- The 0.3.x upgrade path.

v0.4.0    2026-08-06
- Per-member rooms as the only layout. 0.8.0's shared house later superseded this.

v0.3.2    2026-08-02
- memhouse 0.3.2. The tag message is just the version; CHANGELOG.md has only the
  grouped 0.3.x section.

v0.3.1    2026-07-31
- memhouse 0.3.1. The tag message is just the version; CHANGELOG.md has only the
  grouped 0.3.x section.

v0.3.0    2026-07-24
- The first tagged release of the memhouse product line: the 17-adapter shipper, a
  typed ClickHouse schema, the CLI, and the dashboard.


